WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.940
How popular is the Green New Deal, a
sweeping proposal designed to address

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.720
climate change? The proposal, put forward
by Representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.520
and Senator Ed Markey, has
received lots of attention in Washington,

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.160
but a large swath of Americans are not
familiar with it. 41 percent in a mid-February

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.260
online Economist/YouGov poll had heard
nothing at all about it.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.233
Around a quarter – 24 percent – had heard a lot,

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:34.260
and 36 percent a little. In
the same poll, when asked how they felt

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:40.020
about the Green New Deal, people were
split — 23 percent supported it while 24 percent

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.660
were opposed. A substantial 39 percent were
not sure. Rank and file Democrats were more

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.010
enthusiastic than Republicans about the
proposal, with 42 percent of Democrats

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.660
supporting it compared to just 8 percent
of Republicans. A Politico/Morning Consult

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.859
online survey also found deep
partisan divisions. Americans are

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:02.879
increasingly concerned about climate
change, but it is too early to say how

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.440
the Green New Deal will ultimately fare
in the court of public opinion.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.540
How much do you know about the Green New Deal?
Let us know in our poll. Also let us know

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.420
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds and

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:23.180
be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

